SUMMARY:Harvest Festival
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the bounty of autumn with a festival of activities\, music\, demonstrations and more\, led by Duke Gardens and other local groups in the Charlotte Brody Discovery Garden. We’ll have activities for adults and children of all ages together. Children must be accompanied by an adult. \nFee: Free drop-in festival for all ages; no registration required. \nParking: Parking fees apply. \nLocation: Charlotte Brody Discovery Garden (403 on the map). \nAccessibility: This festival takes place outdoors and requires traveling on a combination of paved and unpaved paths with some uneven surfaces and moderate inclines.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/harvest-festival/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens – Charlotte Brody Discovery Garden\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27708\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs,Family programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/1-DG_harvest-festivaltobacco-barn_20251019_KKennedy_A125093.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Sarah P. Duke Gardens
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261020T100000
