UID:17476-1792749600-1792756800@gardens.duke.edu
SUMMARY:Hearty Landscapes: Foodscaping for Joy\, Beauty & Abundance
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to transform any yard\, large or small\, into a beautiful\, productive edible landscape. This presentation with Brittaney Whitenhill of Our-Backyard.org introduces the core principles of foodscaping—integrating vegetables\, herbs\, fruits and pollinator plants into ornamental beds to create landscapes that nourish the body and soul. Participants will discover low-maintenance design strategies\, plant combinations that thrive together and practical tips for maximizing harvests while maintaining curb appeal. Perfect for beginners and seasoned gardeners alike. \nFee: $22; free for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Parking fees apply.   \nLocation:  Pelham-Cullen Classroom inside the Barnes Welcome Center. \nAccessibility: This will be a small group program that takes place partially seated indoors and partially outdoors\, traveling on a combination of paved and unpaved paths with some uneven surfaces and moderate inclines. The indoor location is equipped with a hearing loop\, which transmits sound directly to hearing aids and cochlear implants with a T-coil setting. Accessible restrooms are available onsite.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/hearty-landscapes-foodscaping-for-joy-beauty-abundance/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens–Pelham-Cullen Classroom in the Barnes Welcome Center\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27705\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/Brittaney-Whitenhill-Our-Backyard.org_.jpg
END:VEVENT
